==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Merc & Cat]]s (100%) spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*10 [[Merc & Cat]]s (100%) spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Merc & Cat]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Merc & Cat]]s (100%) spawn, delay 4~10 seconds<sup>120f~300f</sup>.
**10 [[Merc & Cat]]s (100%) spawn, delay 2~5 seconds<sup>60f~150f</sup>.
**30 [[Merc & Cat]]s (100%) spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Merc & Cat]]s (100%) spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Think of this stage like a slightly harder version of Crazed Cow's stage. You'll want to bring a CPU and optionally, a Rich Cat. As for the loadout, you'll need 4-5 cheap meatshields (ex. [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], etc), some spammable Area Attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], and a backliner with good DPS, such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] or a similar Uber Rare. If you've cleared Into the Future, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] will help immensely thanks to his extremely high DPS which can tear through the Merc swarm very easily as long as he is protected well. As for the stage itself, stall the first Merc while upgrading your wallet if you didn't bring a Rich Cat. Once you've got enough money (or the other Mercs start spawning) spawn your attackers to get rid of the Mercs, hit the base, and lure the swarm close to your base. From there, spam everything, and turn on the CPU. Eventually you'll build up a large enough stack to destroy the horde quickly. Once the Merc swarm dies down, you'll be able to reach the enemy base and clear the stage.

